\ port/lab/again.4 - loaded right after port/lab/interp.4: the words of the
\ files before it that the shell runs, compiled again. compile.4 and interp.4
\ are read by the kernel's own interpreter, whose COMPILE, is the kernel's -
\ from here on interp.4's INTERPRET reads, and compile.4's COMPILE, compiles.

BASE @  DECIMAL
\ MOVE: the kernel's copies backwards (CMOVE>, a byte loop in Forth) whenever
\ the source is the lower; only an overlap needs it - else CMOVE, which a
\ design with X_CMOVE runs in C. One R>: a JIT takes the return stack in
\ order down the page only.
: MOVE ( c-addr1 c-addr2 u --- )
  >R 2DUP SWAP - R@ U< R> SWAP IF CMOVE> ELSE CMOVE THEN ;
: WITHIN ( x lo hi --- f )  OVER - >R - R> U< ;
\ relf.4's ABORT": its words reached START by a call, HERE by the kernel's
: (ETYPE) ( c-addr u --- )  ETYPE-XT @ IF ETYPE-XT @XT EXECUTE ELSE 2DROP THEN ;
: (ECHAR) ( c --- )  ABORT-CH C!  ABORT-CH 1 (ETYPE) ;
: (ABORT-MSG) ( c-addr u --- )  (ETYPE) 32 (ECHAR) HERE COUNT (ETYPE) 10 (ECHAR) -2 (THROW) ;
: ABORT" ( "ccc<quote>" --- )
  POSTPONE IF POSTPONE S" POSTPONE (ABORT-MSG) POSTPONE THEN ; IMMEDIATE
BASE !
